nf from node1 (source of truth) to node2, using SSH (enabled sshd on both nodes, generated host keys, deployed the cluster SSH keypair for passwordless auth) and a root cron job on node2 (*/5 * * * *) running /usr/local/sbin/sync-inventory-conf.sh, which rsyncs the file from node1 and only replaces the local copy when content differs (via cmp), logging via syslog. Verified propagation of a real edit within one 5-minute cron tick (well under the 15-minute requirement), both before and after restarting each node. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured healthy baselines (boot_id, sshd/cron active, app.conf checksum) on both nodes, restarted node1 then node2 one at a time (never concurrently), confirmed each node's boot_id and boot time changed after reboot, and confirmed sshd/cron re-activated and the synced file/cron job persisted and continued to sync correctly post-reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered /etc/inventory/app.conf did not exist and created it on node1 as the source-of-truth file\",\"Deployed the cluster SSH keypair to /root/.ssh on node1 and node2 for passwordless inter-node SSH\",\"Diagnosed and fixed sshd failing to start on both nodes (missing host keys via ssh-keygen -A, missing /run/sshd privilege-separation dir) then enabled and started the ssh service on both nodes\",\"Verified passwordless SSH from node2 to node1\",\"Wrote /usr/local/sbin/sync-inventory-conf.sh on node2: rsyncs /etc/inventory/app.conf from node1 under flock, replaces the local copy only if content differs, logs changes via logger\",\"Installed /etc/cron.d/sync-inventory-conf on node2 to run the sync script every 5 minutes; enabled and started the cron service\",\"Verified sync correctness manually, then via an unattended cron tick after changing app.conf on node1 (version=2 change auto-picked up at 09:40:01, confirmed via syslog CRON entry and matching md5sum)\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline evidence (boot_id, boot time, service status, app.conf checksum) on both nodes\",\"Restarted node1 via 'sudo reboot' (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect), polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id/boot time and recovered sshd + app.conf content\",\"Restarted node2 the same way, one at a time after node1 fully recovered, confirmed new boot_id/boot time and recovered sshd, cron service, persisted crontab, and synced app.conf content\",\"Performed a final post-reboot end-to-end test: changed app.conf on node1 (version=3), confirmed node2 automatically synced it at the next cron tick without any manual intervention\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 /etc/inventory/app.conf established as source of truth\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-dec5d22bce29463d\",\"cmd-74a7e27280f64631\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed file absent, then created it on node1 with initial content\"},{\"requirement\":\"Passwordless SSH connectivity node2 -> node1 for sync mechanism\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-09facb64b8e642fc\",\"cmd-a7249ef159244bf7\",\"cmd-011f95db0ed040db\",\"cmd-5fbf084d0c3b4da6\",\"cmd-9465ce39ac2c46f3\",\"cmd-737b37666b3a4c78\"],\"summary\":\"Deployed keys, diagnosed/fixed sshd startup failures on both nodes, verified working passwordless SSH from node2 to node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Sync mechanism installed and functioning (cron + rsync script)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-220f8e2fb2b74f6b\",\"cmd-d3ecb9f610c44737\",\"cmd-27e450fd5c174691\"],\"summary\":\"Created sync script, installed cron.d entry every 5 minutes, ran once manually and confirmed content copied to node2\"},{\"requirement\":\"Change on node1 propagates to node2 within 15 minutes via automated (unattended) cron execution\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-099bef80324c4c7f\",\"cmd-759b3f21d0c14a32\",\"cmd-96260c79142c489b\",\"cmd-6a65806e1ba14c69\"],\"summary\":\"Changed app.conf to version=2 on node1, confirmed node2 still stale, then confirmed automatic sync completed at cron's 09:40:01 tick (syslog CRON log entry) with matching checksum, well within 15 minutes\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-325f348a9e6e4c43\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node1 boot_id, boot time, sshd active status, and app.conf checksum before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-29a0e26cf49c4911\",\"cmd-b8fb7a47ad8d4d32\",\"cmd-84a63bc6d669486b\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged (stream closed), node1 unreachable then reachable again, new boot_id (7eb1486c...) and boot time (09:41) proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart service/data recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-84a63bc6d669486b\"],\"summary\":\"sshd active and app.conf content/checksum intact after reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-51c860b531ac452f\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node2 boot_id, boot time, sshd/cron active status, and app.conf checksum before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-43b332ac94e74ad9\",\"cmd-20ca22fec76340a7\",\"cmd-641b8c801e904dc3\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged (stream closed), node2 unreachable then reachable again, new boot_id (55c25af9...) and boot time (09:41) proving an actual restart occurred; restarted only after node1 had fully recovered, never concurrently\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart service/data/cron persistence and continued sync capability\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-641b8c801e904dc3\",\"cmd-4a714027088545f2\",\"cmd-6da3b8e552a14db8\",\"cmd-6b2654c17985469f\"],\"summary\":\"sshd, cron active and crontab entry persisted after reboot; end-to-end re-test with a fresh change on node1 (version=3) confirmed node2 automatically synced it via cron at the next tick post-reboot\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Set up automated one-way sync of /etc/inventory/app.conf from node1 (source of truth) to node2, using SSH (enabled sshd on both nodes, generated host keys, deployed the cluster SSH keypair for passwordless auth) and a root cron job on node2 (*/5 * * * *) running /usr/local/sbin/sync-inventory-conf.sh, which rsyncs the file from node1 and only replaces the local copy when content differs (via cmp), logging via syslog. Verified propagation of a real edit within one 5-minute cron tick (well under the 15-minute requirement), both before and after restarting each node. Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured healthy baselines (boot_id, sshd/cron active, app.conf checksum) on both nodes, restarted node1 then node2 one at a time (never concurrently), confirmed each node's boot_id and boot time changed after reboot, and confirmed sshd/cron re-activated and the synced file/cron job persisted and continued to sync correctly post-reboot.","actions_performed":["Discovered /etc/inventory/app.conf did not exist and created it on node1 as the source-of-truth file","Deployed the cluster SSH keypair to /root/.ssh on node1 and node2 for passwordless inter-node SSH","Diagnosed and fixed sshd failing to start on both nodes (missing host keys via ssh-keygen -A, missing /run/sshd privilege-separation dir) then enabled and started the ssh service on both nodes","Verified passwordless SSH from node2 to node1","Wrote /usr/local/sbin/sync-inventory-conf.sh on node2: rsyncs /etc/inventory/app.conf from node1 under flock, replaces the local copy only if content differs, logs changes via logger","Installed /etc/cron.d/sync-inventory-conf on node2 to run the sync script every 5 minutes; enabled and started the cron service","Verified sync correctness manually, then via an unattended cron tick after changing app.conf on node1 (version=2 change auto-picked up at 09:40:01, confirmed via syslog CRON entry and matching md5sum)","Captured pre-restart baseline evidence (boot_id, boot time, service status, app.conf checksum) on both nodes","Restarted node1 via 'sudo reboot' (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect), polled until reachable, confirmed new boot_id/boot time and recovered sshd + app.conf content","Restarted node2 the same way, one at a time after node1 fully recovered, confirmed new boot_id/boot time and recovered sshd, cron service, persisted crontab, and synced app.conf content","Performed a final post-reboot end-to-end test: changed app.conf on node1 (version=3), confirmed node2 automatically synced it at the next cron tick without any manual intervention"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 /etc/inventory/app.conf established as source of truth","command_ids":["cmd-dec5d22bce29463d","cmd-74a7e27280f64631"],"summary":"Confirmed file absent, then created it on node1 with initial content"},{"requirement":"Passwordless SSH connectivity node2 -> node1 for sync mechanism","command_ids":["cmd-09facb64b8e642fc","cmd-a7249ef159244bf7","cmd-011f95db0ed040db","cmd-5fbf084d0c3b4da6","cmd-9465ce39ac2c46f3","cmd-737b37666b3a4c78"],"summary":"Deployed keys, diagnosed/fixed sshd startup failures on both nodes, verified working passwordless SSH from node2 to node1"},{"requirement":"Sync mechanism installed and functioning (cron + rsync script)","command_ids":["cmd-220f8e2fb2b74f6b","cmd-d3ecb9f610c44737","cmd-27e450fd5c174691"],"summary":"Created sync script, installed cron.d entry every 5 minutes, ran once manually and confirmed content copied to node2"},{"requirement":"Change on node1 propagates to node2 within 15 minutes via automated (unattended) cron execution","command_ids":["cmd-099bef80324c4c7f","cmd-759b3f21d0c14a32","cmd-96260c79142c489b","cmd-6a65806e1ba14c69"],"summary":"Changed app.conf to version=2 on node1, confirmed node2 still stale, then confirmed automatic sync completed at cron's 09:40:01 tick (syslog CRON log entry) with matching checksum, well within 15 minutes"},{"requirement":"node1 healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-325f348a9e6e4c43"],"summary":"Captured node1 boot_id, boot time, sshd active status, and app.c